{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-38738-r4587283","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Pecan Sweet Potatoes","sourcePageId":38738,"sourceRevision":"4587283","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2025-10-26T23:34:45Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Codename Noreste","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Pecan%20Sweet%20Potatoes&oldid=4587283","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:20:18.668Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Medium Difficulty recipes","Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for dessert","Category:Recipes using almond extract","Category:Recipes using baking powder","Category:Recipes using brown sugar","Category:Recipes using cow milk","Category:Recipes using egg","Category:Recipes using egg white","Category:Recipes using granulated sugar","Category:Recipes using margarine","Category:Recipes using pecan","Category:Recipes using sweet potato","Category:Recipes using wheat flour","Category:Southern U.S. recipes","Category:Texas recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"ad0d8ab976e0bb57c1f171ad3476960cac2592b8e4e0e283201dd2354a137ccf","sourceWikitext":"{{recipesummary|category=Recipes for dessert|servings=Varies|time=60 minutes|difficulty=3}}\n__NOTOC__\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Southern_cuisine |Southern U.S. Cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Texas cuisine|Texas cuisine]]\n\n==Ingredients==\n\n=== Base ===\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] cooked, mashed [[Cookbook:Sweet Potato|sweet potatoes]]\n* ½ stick (4 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|tbsp]]) [[Cookbook:Margarine|margarine]], melted\n* 2 [[Cookbook:Egg|eggs]], beaten (or 3 egg whites)\n* ½ cup [[Cookbook:Milk|milk]] (or ¼ cup skim milk)\n* ⅓–1 cup white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|teaspoon]] [[Cookbook:Vanilla|vanilla]] extract\n* ½ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Almond Extract|almond extract]]\n\n=== Topping ===\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* ½ stick (4 tbsp) margarine, melted\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Flour|flour]] (if using self-rising flour, omit salt and baking powder)\n* ⅛ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Baking Powder|baking powder]]\n* ⅛ teaspoon [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* ½ cup chopped [[Cookbook:Pecan|pecans]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Mix base and topping ingredients in separate bowls.\n# Pour the sweet potato mixture into a 9x12-inch [[Cookbook:Baking Pan|pan]].\n# Sprinkle on topping, and [[Cookbook:Baking|bake]] at 350°F for 45 minutes.\n\n==Notes, tips, and variations==\n\n* Other nuts can be used in the topping—almonds or peanuts serve admirably.\n* Stores well frozen.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for dessert]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sweet potato]]\n[[Category:Recipes using pecan]]\n[[Category:Southern U.S. recipes]]\n[[Category:Texas recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using almond extract]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg white]]\n[[Category:Recipes using wheat flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using margarine]]\n[[Category:Recipes using cow milk]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Pecan Sweet Potatoes","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"3 cups cooked, mashed sweet potatoes","sourceText":"3 cups cooked, mashed sweet potatoes","amountText":